toxic_monkey@hotmail.com (toxic_monkey@hotmail.com) writes:

> How do I set the game to show all my scores when a character dies?  In
> the options menu there is an option called 'scores' that says I can
> set it to 'all' 'around' or 'top' but I don't know how to actually

I didn't see 'all' in the Guidebook or any reference to that kind of
choice in the source.. only top, around and own. Anyway, the syntax for
seeing all your own scores seems to be
OPTIONS=scores:own
IIRC, the default is scores:3 top/2 around
and to keep them and add all your own scores would make the line
OPTIONS=scores:3 top/2 around/own

> Also, how can I view scores w/o killing a character?  Are the scores
> saved in a document somewhere so I can view all of them w/o playing?

The high scores are stored in the file "record" in your playground
directory. In that directory, the command
nethack -s 100
would show top 100, which is the maximum number the game keeps unless it
has been compiled with some compile-time options changed.
Or you could also use my reclist utility that you can download from
http://www.netsonic.fi/~walker/nethack.html

